<|im_start|>user
Problem: Let \( \triangle ABC \) be a triangle with \( AB = 3 \), \( AC = 8 \), \( BC = 7 \). \( M \) and \( N \) are the midpoints of \( \overline{AB} \) and \( \overline{AC} \), respectively. Point \( T \) is selected on side \( BC \) such that \( AT = TC \). The circumcircles of triangles \( BAT \) and \( MAN \) intersect at \( D \). Compute \( DC \).

Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.<|im_end|>
